From: YapLabs <folia@yaplabs.com>
Subject: [PATCH] YaP fastClip treats a corridor chunk as a miss

Level.fastClip calls getChunk on the ray and uses the sections. A cut key
returns null, so an arrow whose clip enters the carved corridor throws.
The hole has no blocks. Treat that chunk as a miss. Not a new splitter.
Post-applyAllPatches.
---

--- a/folia-server/src/minecraft/java/net/minecraft/world/level/Level.java
+++ b/folia-server/src/minecraft/java/net/minecraft/world/level/Level.java
@@ -426,7 +426,12 @@
 
             if ((chunkDiff | chunkYDiff) != 0) {
                 if (chunkDiff != 0) {
-                    lastChunk = level.getChunk(newChunkX, newChunkZ).getSections();
+                    // YaP: a cut key returns null. The corridor is empty, so the clip misses.
+                    if (level instanceof net.minecraft.server.level.ServerLevel yapClipLevel
+                            && io.papermc.paper.threadedregions.YapRegionizerGap.isCutChunk(yapClipLevel, newChunkX, newChunkZ)) {
+                        return miss(clipContext);
+                    }
+                    lastChunk = level.getChunk(newChunkX, newChunkZ).getSections();
                 }
                 final int sectionY = newChunkY - minSection;
                 lastSection = sectionY >= 0 && sectionY < lastChunk.length ? lastChunk[sectionY].getStates() : null;
